{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py | sed -n '35,105p;145,380p;411,433p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/contradictions.py | sed -n '1,180p'; ls -l poc/data/link-pilot-2026-11-21/ledger.json\"","aggregated_output":"    35\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    36\tfrom hivemind import config, live_lock, model, replay, universe       # noqa: E402\n    37\tfrom hivemind.views import judging, store                              # noqa: E402\n    38\tfrom hivemind.views import round as round_module                       # noqa: E402\n    39\timport july_test                                                        # noqa: E402\n    40\timport window_test                                                      # noqa: E402\n    41\t\n    42\tOLD2 = july_test.OLD2\n    43\tITEMS = july_test.ITEMS\n    44\tV118 = REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'\n    45\tV120 = REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v120.json'\n    46\tUNIVERSE = july_test.UNIVERSE\n    47\tWINDOW = ('2026-07-01', '2026-09-20')\n    48\tCALENDAR = ('2026-07-01', '2026-09-20')     # the calendar every sequence must complete, fixed apart from the replay's own window\n    49\tDRAWS = ('1', '2', '3')\n    50\tPINNED = HERE / 'pinned-plan.json'\n    51\tCEILING_LIMIT = 15.0                       # the harness refuses a ceiling above this whatever is passed; Alex names the actual one\n    52\tCOMPARISON = 'Comparison point stated by that judgement: '\n    53\tFORECAST = \"The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): \"\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tdef old2():\n    57\t    return sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\tdef day_of_seq(seq):\n    61\t    return old2().execute('select publication_day from processing_steps where sequence_no=? limit 1', (seq,)).fetchone()[0]\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\tdef opened_at(seq):\n    65\t    \"\"\"The question old-2 opened at `seq` (the link step's candidate `c1` there).\"\"\"\n    66\t    rows = old2().execute('select view_id from views where created_seq=? and view_id in (select view_id from view_keys)', (seq,)).fetchall()\n    67\t    if len(rows) != 1:\n    68\t        raise SystemExit(f'seq {seq}: {len(rows)} number questions opened, expected one')\n    69\t    return rows[0][0]\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\tdef probe_links(draw):\n    73\t    \"\"\"Probe draw <draw>'s proposed links as [(reader, read, sign, seq)], candidate ids resolved to the question old-2 opened there.\"\"\"\n    74\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{REPO / \"poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21\" / f\"probe-v2-{draw}\" / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    75\t    out = []\n    76\t    for seq, record_json in conn.execute(\"select seq, record_json from link_selections where status='proposed' order by id\"):\n    77\t        for p in json.loads(record_json).get('proposed', []):\n    78\t            resolve = (lambda node, s=seq: opened_at(s) if not node.startswith('v') else node)\n    79\t            out.append((resolve(p['reader']), resolve(p['read']), p['sign'], seq))\n    80\t    return out\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\tdef readers(draw):\n    84\t    \"\"\"{reader: its link day}: the day of the article that writes its first link.\"\"\"\n    85\t    days = {}\n    86\t    for reader, _, _, seq in probe_links(draw):\n    87\t        day = day_of_seq(seq)\n    88\t        days[reader] = min(days.get(reader, day), day)\n    89\t    return days\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\tdef retired_rows(reader_days):\n    93\t    \"\"\"The old judge rows of each reader on its link day or later: old-2's accepted judgements by reader and day. Checked: every judge row\n    94\t    of that reader in old-2's archive from the first of them on is in the set (no refused first attempt or other row left behind).\"\"\"\n    95\t    conn, archive = old2(), sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    96\t    rows = {}\n    97\t    for reader, day in reader_days.items():\n    98\t        accepted = [c for (c,) in conn.execute('select call_id from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day>=? order by call_id', (reader, day))]\n    99\t        if not accepted:\n   100\t            continue\n   101\t        family = [c for c, r in archive.execute(\"select call_id, request_json from model_calls where purpose='judge' and call_id>=?\", (accepted[0],))\n   102\t                  if july_test.judged_view(json.loads(r)) == reader]\n   103\t        if sorted(family) != sorted(accepted):\n   104\t            raise SystemExit(f'{reader}: judge rows from call {accepted[0]} on are not exactly its accepted judgements from {day}: '\n   105\t                             f'{sorted(set(family) ^ set(accepted))[:5]}')\n   145\t\n   146\t\n   147\tclass SequenceRun:\n   148\t    \"\"\"One sequence: its transport, its latch, the judging day, the upstream snapshots and the record of every judge attempt.\"\"\"\n   149\t\n   150\t    def __init__(self, kind, draw, inner, folder):\n   151\t        self.kind, self.draw, self.inner, self.folder = kind, draw, inner, folder\n   152\t        self.reader_days = readers(draw)\n   153\t        self.probe = window_test.probe_answers(draw) if kind == 'linked' else {}\n   154\t        self.stored_refusals = window_test.refused_rows()\n   155\t        self.latch = july_test.Latch()\n   156\t        self.day = None\n   157\t        self.attempts, self.refusals_given, self.link_jobs = [], [], []\n   158\t        self.snapshots, self.snapshot_problems, self.snapshot_checks = [], [], 0\n   159\t        self.day_windows, self.terminal = {}, None\n   160\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n   161\t\n   162\t    def transport(self, *args):\n   163\t        request = args[-1]\n   164\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   165\t            if july_test.is_link_request(request) and self.kind == 'linked':\n   166\t                sha = model.request_identity(request)[1]\n   167\t                if sha not in self.probe:\n   168\t                    raise july_test.Stop(f'a link job outside probe draw {self.draw} ({sha[:12]}): not sent')\n   169\t                self.link_jobs.append(sha)\n   170\t                return self.probe[sha]\n   171\t            raise july_test.Stop('a Jev request missed the archive: not sent')\n   172\t        sha = model.request_identity(request)[1]\n   173\t        view_id = july_test.judged_view(request) if is_judgement_request(request) else None\n   174\t        if view_id is not None and view_id not in self.reader_days:\n   175\t            response = self.stored_refusals.pop(sha, None)\n   176\t            if response is not None:\n   177\t                self.refusals_given.append(sha[:12])\n   178\t                return response\n   179\t        day = self.day\n   180\t        allowed = view_id in self.reader_days and day is not None and day >= self.reader_days[view_id]\n   181\t        text = request['messages'][-1]['content']\n   182\t        with self.lock:\n   183\t            self.attempts.append({'view': view_id, 'day': day, 'sha': sha, 'retry': 'Correct it and answer again' in text, 'admitted': allowed})\n   184\t        if allowed:\n   185\t            self.check_snapshot(view_id, day, text)\n   186\t        return self.latch.run(allowed, f'unapproved request on {day} (thesis {view_id}): not sent', (view_id, day),\n   187\t                              lambda: self.inner(*args))\n   188\t\n   189\t    def build_prompt(self, original):\n   190\t        def wrapped(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   191\t            system, user = original(conn, view_id, prompt_version)\n   192\t            reads = {}\n   193\t            for dependency in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\n   194\t                target = dependency['resolved_to']\n   195\t                state = store.current_state(conn, target) if target else None\n   196\t                reads[target] = None if not state else {k: state.get(k) for k in ('judgement_id', 'publication_day', 'rung', 'reasons',\n   197\t                                                                                   'reference', 'implied_outcome')}\n   198\t            with self.lock:\n   199\t                self.snapshots.append({'view': view_id, 'user': user, 'reads': reads, 'day': self.day})\n   200\t            return system, user\n   201\t        return wrapped\n   202\t\n   203\t    def check_snapshot(self, view_id, day, text):\n   204\t        \"\"\"Each dependency entry of the request, found by its own target id, is rendered from that dependency's conclusion recorded when\n   205\t        the prompt was built: its judgement day in the header, its comparison point, forecast and reasons excerpt line for line (a retry\n   206\t        carries the same prompt with the correction lines after it).\"\"\"\n   207\t        with self.lock:\n   208\t            built = [s for s in self.snapshots if s['view'] == view_id and text.startswith(s['user'])]\n   209\t        if not built:\n   210\t            if self.kind == 'linked':\n   211\t                self.snapshot_problems.append((view_id, day, 'no prompt recorded for this request'))\n   212\t            return\n   213\t        reads = built[-1]['reads']\n   214\t        if self.kind == 'linked' and not reads:\n   215\t            self.snapshot_problems.append((view_id, day, 'a linked reader request with no dependency recorded'))\n   216\t        lines = text.split('\\n')\n   217\t        checked = False\n   218\t        for target, state in reads.items():\n   219\t            if state is None:\n   220\t                continue\n   221\t            headers = [i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if line.startswith(f'- {target} (')]\n   222\t            if len(headers) != 1:\n   223\t                self.snapshot_problems.append((view_id, day, f'{target}: {len(headers)} dependency entries'))\n   224\t                continue\n   225\t            i = headers[0]\n   226\t            expected = [f'    {COMPARISON}{judging._indented(state.get(\"reference\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   227\t                        f'    {FORECAST}{judging._indented(state.get(\"implied_outcome\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   228\t                        f'    Reasons (excerpt): {judging._indented((state.get(\"reasons\") or \"\")[:600])}']\n   229\t            block = '\\n'.join(lines[i + 1:])\n   230\t            if not lines[i].endswith(f', judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}') or not block.startswith('\\n'.join(expected)):\n   231\t                self.snapshot_problems.append((view_id, day, f'{target}: entry is not its latest conclusion at prompt time '\n   232\t                                                              f'(judgement {state[\"judgement_id\"]})'))\n   233\t            checked = True\n   234\t        if checked:\n   235\t            with self.lock:\n   236\t                self.snapshot_checks += 1\n   237\t\n   238\t    def judge_day(self, original):\n   239\t        def wrapped(conn, archive_, cfg_, day, seq, **keywords):\n   240\t            before = archive_.conn.execute('select coalesce(max(call_id), 0) from model_calls').fetchone()[0]\n   241\t            self.day = day\n   242\t            try:\n   243\t                result = original(conn, archive_, cfg_, day, seq, **keywords)\n   244\t            finally:\n   245\t                self.day = None\n   246\t                after = archive_.conn.execute('select coalesce(max(call_id), 0) from model_calls').fetchone()[0]\n   247\t                self.day_windows[day] = (before, after)\n   248\t            failed = getattr(result, 'failed', None)\n   249\t            if failed and self.terminal is None:\n   250\t                text = str(failed)\n   251\t                view = text.split('judgement refused twice: ', 1)[1].split(':', 1)[0] if 'judgement refused twice: ' in text else None\n   252\t                self.terminal = ({'outcome': 'double refusal', 'view': view, 'day': day, 'reader': view in self.reader_days}\n   253\t                                 if view else {'outcome': 'infrastructure stop', 'day': day, 'reason': text[:300]})\n   254\t            return result\n   255\t        return wrapped\n   256\t\n   257\t\n   258\tdef prepare(folder, kind, draw):\n   259\t    if folder.exists():\n   260\t        raise SystemExit(f'{folder} exists: a sequence starts from an empty folder and is never resumed')\n   261\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True)\n   262\t    shutil.copyfile(OLD2 / 'archive.sqlite', folder / 'archive.sqlite')\n   263\t    archive = model.Archive(str(folder / 'archive.sqlite'))\n   264\t    top = archive.conn.execute('select coalesce(max(call_id), 0) from model_calls').fetchone()[0]\n   265\t    retired = []\n   266\t    if kind == 'control':\n   267\t        for reader, calls in retired_rows(readers(draw)).items():\n   268\t            for call_id in calls:\n   269\t                archive.retire(call_id)\n   270\t                retired.append((reader, call_id))\n   271\t    views = folder / 'views.sqlite'\n   272\t    marker = sqlite3.connect(views)\n   273\t    marker.execute('create table harness_only (name text, day text)')\n   274\t    marker.execute(\"insert into harness_only values ('paid_run.py', '2026-11-21')\")\n   275\t    marker.commit()\n   276\t    marker.close()\n   277\t    return archive, top, retired\n   278\t\n   279\t\n   280\tdef trajectory_check(views, reader_set):\n   281\t    \"\"\"H2: every non-reader judgement equal to old-2's by question and day (the request and every substantive field); every other table\n   282\t    equal, typed keys included.\"\"\"\n   283\t    built, stored = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{views}?mode=ro', uri=True), old2()\n   284\t    fields = ('view_id, publication_day, rung, reasons, reference, implied_outcome, cited_evidence_json, cited_views_json, pushes_json, '\n   285\t              'theme_pushes_json, changed, why_changed, request_sha256')\n   286\t\n   287\t    def rows(conn):\n   288\t        return sorted(tuple(r) for r in conn.execute(f'select {fields} from judgements') if r[0] not in reader_set)\n   289\t    tables = {'non-reader judgements': rows(built) == rows(stored)}\n   290\t    for name, sql in {'views': 'select view_id, question, created_seq from views',\n   291\t                      'view_keys': 'select view_id, measure, scope, period_start, period_end, unit from view_keys',\n   292\t                      'evidence': 'select evidence_id, quote, created_seq from evidence',\n   293\t                      'evidence_links': 'select evidence_id, view_id, seq from evidence_links',\n   294\t                      'rungs': 'select view_id, position, label, condition, lo, hi from rungs',\n   295\t                      'view_switches': 'select view_id, open, reason, after_seq from view_switches',\n   296\t                      'successions': 'select view_id, succeeds, seq from successions'}.items():\n   297\t        tables[name] = sorted(tuple(r) for r in built.execute(sql)) == sorted(tuple(r) for r in stored.execute(sql))\n   298\t    return {f'{k} equal': v for k, v in tables.items()}\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\tdef run_sequence(out, kind, draw, inner, ledger_state, transport_kind):\n   302\t    if kind not in ('linked', 'control') or draw not in DRAWS:\n   303\t        raise SystemExit('kind must be linked or control, draw 1, 2 or 3')\n   304\t    pinned = pinned_plan(draw)\n   305\t    folder = out / f'{kind}-{draw}'\n   306\t    archive, top, retired = prepare(folder, kind, draw)\n   307\t    run = SequenceRun(kind, draw, inner, folder)\n   308\t    cfg = config.load(str(V120 if kind == 'linked' else V118))\n   309\t    summary = {'kind': kind, 'draw': draw, 'transport': transport_kind, 'config': cfg.version, 'archive_top': top,\n   310\t               'reader days': run.reader_days, 'retired rows': len(retired), 'stopped': ''}\n   311\t    original_judge_day, original_build = round_module.judge_day, judging.build_prompt\n   312\t    round_module.judge_day, judging.build_prompt = run.judge_day(original_judge_day), run.build_prompt(original_build)\n   313\t    held = live_lock.acquire(str(folder / 'views.sqlite'))\n   314\t    try:\n   315\t        replay.run(testdb_path=str(ITEMS), views_path=str(folder / 'views.sqlite'), archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=universe.load(str(UNIVERSE)),\n   316\t                   from_day=WINDOW[0], until_day=WINDOW[1], transport=run.transport, log=lambda *a: None, only_objects={'NVDA'})\n   317\t    except Exception as error:\n   318\t        summary['stopped'] = f'{type(error).__name__}: {error}'[:500]\n   319\t        if run.terminal is None:\n   320\t            run.terminal = {'outcome': 'infrastructure stop', 'reason': summary['stopped']}\n   321\t    finally:\n   322\t        live_lock.release(held)\n   323\t        round_module.judge_day, judging.build_prompt = original_judge_day, original_build\n   324\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   325\t    reader_judgements = [dict(zip(('view', 'day', 'call_id', 'judgement_id'), r)) for r in conn.execute(\n   326\t        'select view_id, publication_day, call_id, judgement_id from judgements where view_id in (%s) order by judgement_id'\n   327\t        % ','.join('?' * len(pinned['readers'])), tuple(pinned['readers']))]\n   328\t    for j in reader_judgements:\n   329\t        window = run.day_windows.get(j['day'], (None, None))\n   330\t        j['must be fresh'] = j['day'] >= pinned['readers'][j['view']]\n   331\t        j['fresh on its day'] = window[0] is not None and window[0] < j['call_id'] <= window[1]\n   332\t        j['from the archive'] = j['call_id'] <= top\n   333\t    archive_conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   334\t    attempt_rows = []\n   335\t    for call_id, request_json, sha in archive_conn.execute(\"select call_id, request_json, request_sha256 from model_calls where purpose='judge' and call_id > ?\", (top,)):\n   336\t        view = july_test.judged_view(json.loads(request_json))\n   337\t        day = next((d for d, (b, a) in run.day_windows.items() if b < call_id <= a), None)\n   338\t        attempt_rows.append({'call_id': call_id, 'view': view, 'day': day, 'refused': ':refused:' in sha, 'reader': view in pinned['readers']})\n   339\t    committed = sorted(list(r) for r in conn.execute(\"select view_id, depends_on, direction, seq from dependencies where kind='reads'\"))\n   340\t    days_completed = [r[0] for r in conn.execute('select day from days_completed order by seq')]\n   341\t    with open(folder / 'snapshots.jsonl', 'w') as handle:\n   342\t        for snapshot in run.snapshots:\n   343\t            handle.write(json.dumps({'view': snapshot['view'], 'day': snapshot['day'], 'reads': snapshot['reads']}) + '\\n')\n   344\t    summary.update({\n   345\t        'terminal': run.terminal or {'outcome': 'complete'},\n   346\t        'days completed': days_completed,\n   347\t        'links committed': committed,\n   348\t        'link jobs consumed': sorted(run.link_jobs),\n   349\t        'judge attempts at the transport': run.attempts,\n   350\t        'archive judge rows written (dated)': attempt_rows,\n   351\t        'stored refusals given back': run.refusals_given,\n   352\t        'reader judgements': reader_judgements,\n   353\t        'snapshot problems': run.snapshot_problems, 'snapshot checks': run.snapshot_checks,\n   354\t        'trajectory (H2)': trajectory_check(folder / 'views.sqlite', set(pinned['readers'])),\n   355\t        'latch': run.latch.reason, 'ledger': ledger_state(),\n   356\t    })\n   357\t    summary['acceptance'] = acceptance(summary, pinned, kind)\n   358\t    (folder / 'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   359\t    return summary\n   360\t\n   361\t\n   362\tdef acceptance(summary, pinned, kind):\n   363\t    \"\"\"The one gate for the dry runs and the paid send.\"\"\"\n   364\t    judgements = summary['reader judgements']\n   365\t    checks = {\n   366\t        'window completed, no stop': summary['stopped'] == '' and summary['terminal'] == {'outcome': 'complete'},\n   367\t        'calendar completed (every day old-2 completed)': summary.get('days completed') == planned_days(),\n   368\t        'committed graph equals the pinned one (labels included)': summary['links committed'] == (pinned['graph'] if kind == 'linked' else []),\n   369\t        'probe jobs consumed exactly the pinned set': summary['link jobs consumed'] == (pinned['probe jobs'] if kind == 'linked' else []),\n   370\t        'every post-link reader judgement fresh on its own day': all(j['fresh on its day'] for j in judgements if j['must be fresh']),\n   371\t        'every pre-link reader judgement from the archive': all(j['from the archive'] for j in judgements if not j['must be fresh']),\n   372\t        'reader judgements present': bool(judgements),\n   373\t        'upstream snapshot clean': not summary['snapshot problems'],\n   374\t        'upstream snapshot exercised (linked)': kind == 'control' or summary['snapshot checks'] > 0,\n   375\t        'fixed trajectory (H2)': all(summary['trajectory (H2)'].values()),\n   376\t        'ledger clean (not stopped, no overrun)': not (summary.get('ledger') or {}).get('stopped') and not (summary.get('ledger') or {}).get('overrun'),\n   377\t    }\n   378\t    return dict(checks, accepted=all(checks.values()))\n   379\t\n   380\t\n   411\tdef send(out, kind, draw, ledger_path, approved):\n   412\t    budget = july_test.budget_module()\n   413\t    if not (isinstance(approved, float) and math.isfinite(approved) and 0 < approved <= CEILING_LIMIT):\n   414\t        raise SystemExit('the approved ceiling must be a finite amount above 0 (and within the harness limit)')\n   415\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path))\n   416\t    ceiling = ledger.read()['ceiling']\n   417\t    if not (isinstance(ceiling, (int, float)) and math.isfinite(ceiling) and ceiling == approved):\n   418\t        raise SystemExit(f'the ledger ceiling {ceiling!r} is not the approved ${approved}: refused')\n   419\t    label = f'{kind}-{draw}'\n   420\t    lock_handle = open(Path(ledger_path).with_name(f'{label}.launcher.lock'), 'a+')\n   421\t    if not ledger.claim_launcher(label, lock_handle):\n   422\t        raise SystemExit(f'another launch of {label} is running')\n   423\t    budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   424\t    try:\n   425\t        summary = run_sequence(out, kind, draw, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger.read, 'paid')\n   426\t    finally:\n   427\t        ledger.remove_launcher(label)\n   428\t    print(json.dumps({'sequence': label, 'terminal': summary['terminal'], 'stopped': summary['stopped'][:300],\n   429\t                      'ledger': summary['ledger'], **summary['acceptance']}, indent=1))\n   430\t    return summary['acceptance']['accepted']\n   431\t\n   432\t\n   433\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n     1\t\"\"\"The primary line P of the paid comparison (PAID-DESIGN.md §4): per store, for each calendar date from the link day to the window's\n     2\tend on which both the Data Center question and the total revenue question (FY2027) hold a conclusion, compare their annual forecasts.\n     3\t\n     4\tEach question's conclusion on a date is its last accepted judgement on or before that date (carried forward). Its annual forecast is\n     5\tan amount or range in its `implied_outcome` between $200B and $1,000B, chosen by `annual` (the last one followed by \"FY2027\", else one\n     6\topening the text, else the last one): a range (\"$400–410B\", \"$390 billion to $395 billion\") gives its low and high ends; a single\n     7\tamount gives both. A date is\n     8\t  definite:  the segment's low end exceeds the company's high end (the part above the whole whatever the range);\n     9\t  overlap:   the two ranges share some value without the part being wholly above (reported, not counted as a contradiction);\n    10\t  clear:     the segment's high end is at or below the company's low end;\n    11\t  ambiguous: either forecast fell to the last-amount rule with several distinct amounts (reported, read by hand);\n    12\t  unparsed:  either forecast has no amount in that band.\n    13\tCoverage = parsed dates / dates with both conclusions.\n    14\t\n    15\t  python3 contradictions.py <views.sqlite> [<dc view> <total view>] [--from 2026-07-10] [--rows]\n    16\t\"\"\"\n    17\timport re\n    18\timport sqlite3\n    19\timport sys\n    20\t\n    21\tUNIT = r'(?:B\\b|bn\\b|billion\\b)'\n    22\tNUMBER = r'(\\d{1,4}(?:,\\d{3})*(?:\\.\\d+)?)'\n    23\tRANGE = re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUMBER + r'\\s?' + UNIT + r'?\\s?(?:–|—|-|to)\\s?\\$?\\s?' + NUMBER + r'\\s?' + UNIT, re.I)\n    24\tSINGLE = re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUMBER + r'\\s?' + UNIT, re.I)\n    25\tBAND = (200.0, 1000.0)\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef value(text):\n    29\t    return float(text.replace(',', ''))\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\tYEAR = re.compile(r'^[^.;$]{0,30}?\\b(?:for |in )?(?:FY ?2027|fiscal 2027|fiscal year 2027)', re.I)\n    33\tLEADING = 30\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\tdef amounts(text):\n    37\t    \"\"\"Every amount or range in the band: [(start, end, (low, high))], ranges taking precedence over the amounts inside them.\"\"\"\n    38\t    found = []\n    39\t    for match in RANGE.finditer(text or ''):\n    40\t        low, high = value(match.group(1)), value(match.group(2))\n    41\t        if BAND[0] <= low <= BAND[1] and BAND[0] <= high <= BAND[1] and low <= high:\n    42\t            found.append((match.start(), match.end(), (low, high)))\n    43\t    for match in SINGLE.finditer(text or ''):\n    44\t        amount = value(match.group(1))\n    45\t        if BAND[0] <= amount <= BAND[1] and not any(start <= match.start() < end for start, end, _ in found):\n    46\t            found.append((match.start(), match.end(), (amount, amount)))\n    47\t    return sorted(found)\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef annual(text):\n    51\t    \"\"\"(low, high, how) of the annual forecast, or None: the last amount followed within 30 characters by \"FY2027\" (or \"fiscal\n    52\t    2027\"); else an amount opening the text (within its first 30 characters); else the last amount, marked ambiguous when the text\n    53\t    holds more than one distinct amount in the band.\"\"\"\n    54\t    found = amounts(text)\n    55\t    if not found:\n    56\t        return None\n    57\t    named = [f for f in found if YEAR.match(text[f[1]:])]\n    58\t    if named:\n    59\t        return (*named[-1][2], 'year')\n    60\t    if found[0][0] <= LEADING:\n    61\t        return (*found[0][2], 'leading')\n    62\t    return (*found[-1][2], 'last' if len({f[2] for f in found}) == 1 else 'ambiguous')\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef classify(segment, company):\n    66\t    if segment is None or company is None:\n    67\t        return 'unparsed'\n    68\t    if 'ambiguous' in (segment[2], company[2]):\n    69\t        return 'ambiguous'\n    70\t    if segment[0] > company[1]:\n    71\t        return 'definite'\n    72\t    if segment[1] <= company[0]:\n    73\t        return 'clear'\n    74\t    return 'overlap'\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef pair(conn):\n    78\t    \"\"\"The FY2027 Data Center and total revenue questions of a store, by their typed keys.\"\"\"\n    79\t    keys = conn.execute('select view_id, measure, scope, period_start from view_keys').fetchall()\n    80\t    segment = [k[0] for k in keys if k[1] == 'segment_revenue' and 'data center' in (k[2] or '').lower() and k[3] == '2026-02-01']\n    81\t    company = [k[0] for k in keys if k[1] == 'total_revenue' and k[3] == '2026-02-01']\n    82\t    return (segment[0] if segment else None), (company[0] if company else None)\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tdef daily(conn, segment_view, company_view, from_day='2026-07-10', until_day='2026-09-20'):\n    86\t    \"\"\"[(date, class, segment range, company range, segment text, company text)] for every calendar date in the span on which both\n    87\t    questions hold a conclusion.\"\"\"\n    88\t    import datetime\n    89\t    rows = {}\n    90\t    for view_id in (segment_view, company_view):\n    91\t        rows[view_id] = conn.execute('select publication_day, implied_outcome from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id',\n    92\t                                     (view_id,)).fetchall()\n    93\t    out = []\n    94\t    day = datetime.date.fromisoformat(from_day)\n    95\t    end = datetime.date.fromisoformat(until_day)\n    96\t    while day <= end:\n    97\t        iso = day.isoformat()\n    98\t        latest = {}\n    99\t        for view_id, judgements in rows.items():\n   100\t            held = [text for published, text in judgements if published <= iso]\n   101\t            latest[view_id] = held[-1] if held else None\n   102\t        if latest[segment_view] is not None and latest[company_view] is not None:\n   103\t            segment, company = annual(latest[segment_view]), annual(latest[company_view])\n   104\t            out.append((iso, classify(segment, company), segment, company, latest[segment_view], latest[company_view]))\n   105\t        day += datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n   106\t    return out\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\tdef summary(rows):\n   110\t    counts = {name: sum(1 for r in rows if r[1] == name) for name in ('definite', 'overlap', 'clear', 'ambiguous', 'unparsed')}\n   111\t    counts['dates'] = len(rows)\n   112\t    counts['coverage'] = round((len(rows) - counts['unparsed'] - counts['ambiguous']) / len(rows), 3) if rows else 0.0\n   113\t    return counts\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\tdef main(argv):\n   117\t    path = argv[0]\n   118\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   119\t    positional = [a for a in argv[1:] if not a.startswith('--')]\n   120\t    segment_view, company_view = positional[:2] if len(positional) >= 2 else pair(conn)\n   121\t    from_day = argv[argv.index('--from') + 1] if '--from' in argv else '2026-07-10'\n   122\t    rows = daily(conn, segment_view, company_view, from_day)\n   123\t    print(path, segment_view, company_view, summary(rows))\n   124\t    if '--rows' in argv:\n   125\t        for row in rows:\n   126\t            print(row[0], row[1], row[2], row[3], '|', (row[4] or '')[:100].replace('\\n', ' '), '||', (row[5] or '')[:100].replace('\\n', ' '))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   130\t    main(sys.argv[1:])\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  292 Nov 21 16:00 poc/data/link-pilot-2026-11-21/ledger.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md | sed -n '41,102p;158,175p;201,250p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/round37-brief.md | tail -35; tail -18 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\"","aggregated_output":"    41\t## 2. Harness rules (July's, `dependency-design/july_test.py`, extended to the window)\n    42\t\n    43\t- Harness-only marker, the store lock, never resumed; a stop is final, and its verdict follows §4's precedence (a linked double refusal\n    44\t  fails; an infrastructure stop or a control's double refusal makes the comparison inconclusive).\n    45\t- **Allow-list before the budget transport, per sequence, under July's latch** (admission and the inner call under one lock; the first\n    46\t  refusal closes the sequence): a linked sequence may buy only judge requests of its readers on days at or after their D_R; a control\n    47\t  only the retired readers' judge requests on those days; a link job only from the probe draw. Admission is bound to the replay's\n    48\t  judging day (the harness wraps `round.judge_day` to know the day of every judge request), not to the request's text. Any other request that misses the archive\n    49\t  stops the sequence (round 22 found no legitimate non-reader change on this trajectory). The four answers old-2's own run refused are\n    50\t  given back once each for non-readers, as in the `neither` pass.\n    51\t- Settlement at published rates with cache writes at 1.25x; reservation from request size (D696).\n    52\t\n    53\t## 3. The $0 proofs before the send\n    54\t\n    55\t1. `v120-replay` (done): poc-v120 with each probe draw's own answers meets all 17 link jobs and ends equal to old-2.\n    56\t2. **Linked dry run per draw** (a fake judge answering readers with markers): committed links equal probe draw n's proposals; no link\n    57\t   job outside the probe; no circle correction; every non-reader judgement equal to old-2's by question and day in its request and its\n    58\t   substantive fields (rung, reasons, reference, implied outcome, cites); **freshness checked on the archive side as well as the\n    59\t   transport side** (round 23: a cache hit bypasses the transport): every reader judgement made on a day at or after its D_R has a call\n    60\t   id above the copied archive's top, and none before; **the upstream snapshot:** when each reader prompt is built, the harness records\n    61\t   the judgement id, date, reference and forecast of each question it reads (wrapping `store.current_state` as `judging.build_prompt`\n    62\t   calls it) and checks the rendered dependency block against that snapshot, never against the final ledger; the cases a same-day\n    63\t   upstream update, a carried-forward upstream answer (old-2's v14 has ten judgement days with no v8 judgement that day) and a refused\n    64\t   upstream answer followed by its accepted retry are each exercised; the added days listed.\n    65\t3. **Control dry run per draw:** the retired rows listed and checked; only the retired readers reach the transport, on the right days;\n    66\t   every other judgement equal to old-2's by question and day.\n    67\t4. The stop paths and the latch race, on the window.\n    68\t5. Price from old-2's archived usage of the readers' days (round 22: 247 judgements, $0.872 a sequence) plus the dry runs' added days,\n    69\t   prompt growth from the dependency block, retries, and the live reservations, each shown apart.\n    70\t\n    71\t## 4. Reading rule (frozen before the send)\n    72\t\n    73\t**Unit:** a calendar date of the fixed window 07-10..09-20 (73 dates); on each, each question's conclusion is its last accepted\n    74\tjudgement on or before the date, carried forward. A date's class comes from the **distinct answer pair** (v9's and v14's answers) in\n    75\tforce that day.\n    76\t\n    77\t**Hand classification of every distinct pair (round 23):** `contradictions.py` orders the work (definite and ambiguous first); every\n    78\tdistinct pair in all six sequences is read by hand against both answers and classed **definite** (Data Center's annual low end above\n    79\ttotal revenue's high end, as each answer finally states its FY2027 forecast), **overlap**, **clear**, or **unresolved** (an answer\n    80\tstates no FY2027 forecast that can be read). A parser class that the reading changes is recorded as a misparse with its corrected\n    81\tclass. Dates inherit their pair's class. Before reading, the pairs are listed per sequence with their date spans.\n    82\t\n    83\t**Primary line, P, per pair n (round 24: three outcomes):** over all 73 dates, each arm's dates are definite (D), not definite\n    84\t(overlap or clear, N) or unresolved (U), each date keeping its own arm's class even where the other arm is unresolved. Linked-n's\n    85\tdefinite count lies between D_L and D_L + U_L; control-n's between D_C and D_C + U_C.\n    86\t- **Improved:** D_L + U_L < D_C (the least favourable completion still has fewer definite dates in the linked arm).\n    87\t- **Not improved:** D_L >= D_C + U_C (even the most favourable completion cannot give the linked arm fewer).\n    88\t- **Undecided:** otherwise (the unresolved dates could change the result).\n    89\t- **Testable:** D_C >= 2 (known definite dates of the control over all 73, not only dates readable in both arms).\n    90\t- **Readable:** each arm has at least 60 of the 73 dates resolved **in the hand-read classes** (before any credit adjustment): a\n    91\t  coverage policy that deliberately allows at most 13 unreadable dates per arm (82.2%). A readable forecast with unsupported arithmetic\n    92\t  stays readable; its uncertainty reaches P through the credit-adjusted classes the bounds use.\n    93\t- **Credit (rounds 24–25; one rule):** a **gain** is a date on which the linked arm is not definite and the control is definite. Only\n    94\t  gains are ever adjusted; no other date's class changes for credit. When a pair is provisionally improved, **every** gain is reviewed:\n    95\t  both linked answers in force on it (v9's and v14's), deduplicated by judgement id, are read for July's rule B (arithmetic following\n    96\t  from stated inputs; each assumption that sizes the result disclosed and supported) and for H4. A gain whose forecasts carry a material\n    97\t  rule-B failure on which its reconciliation rests earns no credit (counted definite for P). A gain resting on an unsupported CPU\n    98\t  increment: when the increment can be quantified, the forecast with it removed gives the gain's credit-adjusted class; when it cannot,\n    99\t  the gain counts unresolved: **every** such gain of the pair is marked unresolved, and the bounds are then recomputed once across the\n   100\t  pair (round 26: two gains marked one at a time could each look harmless). Each date keeps its actual class in the report beside its\n   101\t  credit-adjusted class; P is recomputed on the credit-adjusted classes. A confirmed CPU double count stays a harm (H4) whatever its\n   102\t  date.\n   158\treaders, apart from the run's three hours.\n   159\t\n   160\t**Reported beside, not gating:** each link's relation, direction and sign (the weak CPU link disclosed); self-made references\n   161\t(`reference_census.py`'s measures, the `unsourced` scan with the dependency block excluded); v14 linked against control; v21's implied\n   162\ttotal against v9 and v14; linked-only judgement days.\n   163\t\n   164\t## 5. Cost (estimate; the ceiling is Alex's)\n   165\t\n   166\tReader judgements from their links, at published rates from old-2's archived usage: $0.872 a sequence (247 judgements, round 22).\n   167\tLinked sequences: about 19 added judgement days each (round 22's count on the fixed schedule; the dry runs give the exact count) and\n   168\tthe dependency block's prompt growth (about 10%): about $1.05. Three linked and three controls: about $5.8, plus retries and refusals\n   169\t(about 5%) and the live reservations (one judge call per sequence at once). Priced exactly from the dry runs before the ceiling\n   170\tquestion.\n   171\t\n   172\t## 6. Time\n   173\t\n   174\tOne paid call at a time per sequence: about 270–300 calls; old-2's stored reader calls took a median 38.2 seconds (round 23), so about\n   175\t3 hours with replay and retries, the six sequences at once.\n   201\t## 8. Staged send (D708, council round 31)\n   202\t\n   203\tPair 1 (linked-1, control-1) is registered as pair 1 of this comparison and sent first, its two arms together, on the pinned graph and\n   204\tretirement plan; its stores, archives, snapshots and summaries are kept. Its reading (`worksheet.py build-pilot`, `verdict.py --pilot`):\n   205\tthe blind P rows of both arms read by hand and bound to the stores' pairs; H4 on every post-link v14 answer of linked-1; H1 from the\n   206\tdated summaries; the gain review when the pair is provisionally improved. The pilot's decision, by §4's precedence: a linked double\n   207\trefusal fails; an invalid run, coverage short or control-1 under 2 definite dates is inconclusive; an H1 or H4 harm stops; \"improved\"\n   208\tafter the gain review continues to pairs 2 and 3 and the full reading (pair 1's remaining readings done then under the same rule);\n   209\t\"not improved\" or \"undecided\" stops, each with its reason. The pilot never gives the comparison's pass, which needs three pairs. H3's\n   210\tselector and H5's duplicate counting (round 30) are fixed before the full reading, not before the pilot. Pilot cost about $1.96; the\n   211\tceiling is Alex's (about $2.50 proposed).\n    30\t   one edit from any of its 124 listed ids, its retry 8809 accepted; 8938 `e362`; 8941 `e3111`), one of them a retry. Readers cite\n    31\t   long lists (v21 cites 29, v14 sees 124), which plausibly raises their rate. Census script: `scratchpad/id_typo_census.py`.\n    32\t4. In control (poc-v118), no dependencies exist and none of the 118 fresh v9/v14 requests mentions v21: v21's conclusion feeds neither\n    33\t   question of the primary line P (v9 Data Center, v14 total revenue).\n    34\t5. The ordering tool (`contradictions.py`, a lead, not a reading) on 07-10..09-07: control-1 28 definite of 60 dates, old-2 50 of 60.\n    35\t   The class recurs in the fresh control.\n    36\t6. linked-1 (poc-v120) is still running at the time of writing; its outcome will be added below before you answer.\n    37\t\n    38\t## The registered rule\n    39\t\n    40\tPAID-DESIGN.md §2: \"a stop is final, and its verdict follows §4's precedence (a linked double refusal fails; an infrastructure stop or\n    41\ta control's double refusal makes the comparison inconclusive)\". §4 precedence (2): \"a control's double refusal … → inconclusive\". §8:\n    42\t\"an invalid run … is inconclusive\". The product itself on a double refusal: `judge_day` records `judgement_refused_twice` and the day\n    43\t\"remains resumable\"; a resume re-samples (the refused rows are retired).\n    44\t\n    45\t## Questions\n    46\t\n    47\t1. Is the registered pilot verdict \"inconclusive (invalid: control double refusal)\" — or \"fail\" if linked-1 double-refuses — exactly\n    48\t   what the rules give? Anything I have misread?\n    49\t2. Is the mechanism right (one-character id copy errors, a product defect of the frozen judge, unrelated to the links)? Is the census\n    50\t   right and complete on the stored runs?\n    51\t3. The design treats a double refusal as terminal, while the product treats it as a resumable day. With about 200 reader attempts per\n    52\t   sequence, a double refusal in some sequence of six is not rare. Should the rule for the remaining comparison change, and to what?\n    53\t   Candidate (mine): on a double refusal in either arm, the day is resumed once, as the product does (the refused rows retired, the\n    54\t   refusals counted in H1); a second double refusal on the same day is terminal under the old precedence. Recorded before any further\n    55\t   send. Counter-arguments: selection, a rule changed after a result, the symmetry between arms.\n    56\t4. The next step for Alex (he is active; any spend beyond the $2.50 ceiling is his). Options I see:\n    57\t   A. Stop the line with the inconclusive verdict.\n    58\t   B. Re-draw control-1 from scratch under the current rules (about $0.85, a new ceiling; the same risk again).\n    59\t   C. Resume control-1 from 09-08 under the candidate rule (about $0.15 inside the current ceiling), then read pair 1 as registered.\n    60\t   Which one, and what result of it would move the decision? If C, is it legitimate for pair 1 given that I have seen control-1's\n    61\t   lead count (item 5) but not linked-1's P rows?\n    62\t5. Should the id copy error itself go to Alex as a product finding (one structural rule), and what would that rule be (for example,\n    63\t   evidence cited by a short list position the code maps back, or the retry note naming the nearest listed ids)? It is a change to the\n    64\t   frozen judge, a new version only Alex opens.\n| 24 | 11-04 夜 | 第二处：资本开支题的说明加\"资本开支也等于同期经营现金流减自由现金流（按通常的定义）\"；两轮独立复核后补到 14 篇、门槛写死；冻结后发 84 次（0.148 美元） | 没过：现金流那句原样 0/3 没写，加一句后只写了 1/3（且一句话里写出推算的 17 亿）；B–D 没触发；F 失败——一篇 Vera CPU 文章里加一句后三次都改写引用被拒、Perplexity 两次挂到总收入题（与资本开支无关，请求一变整段输出跟着变）。**根子**：营业利润率那句（i163）和现金流那句（i131）在冻结的抽取金标里都是\"已签版 excluded（§5.3 已知事实的重述）、待批第 6 条 optional\"；冻结提示词的复核也教模型\"重述的老情况是杂音\"；而读者 B 判这两道题正是拿它们当现状起点。窗口在五月财报之后才开始，账本里没有更早的记录——冷启动缺口。不是挂题或引用的问题 | 交 Alex：覆盖开始时公司最近一期已公布的数从哪来（第 6 条提议，或覆盖开始时一次性记下基线）；两处小改动都停 |\n| 25 | 11-05 凌晨 | Alex：\"乙\"（D363）：开始跟踪时从公司最近一期财报一次性记下每道题的起点数 | 找到的材料：5 月 20 日的第一季度 8-K 附件 99.1 新闻稿；清洗后的文字丢了财务表，原始网页文字（20,790 字符）里有营业利润（会计准则 535.36 亿、调整后 537.83 亿）、购置固定资产 17.57 亿、经营现金流 503.44 亿、自由现金流 485.54 亿；10-Q 原始文字也有（营业利润占收入 65.6%）但长且杂。最简单的验证：不改任何提示词，把新闻稿当开始跟