{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/round37-brief.md | tail -10; rg -n 'cites|pushes' src/hivemind/views/judging.py | head -18; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '1,33p'\"","aggregated_output":"    55\t   send. Counter-arguments: selection, a rule changed after a result, the symmetry between arms.\n    56\t4. The next step for Alex (he is active; any spend beyond the $2.50 ceiling is his). Options I see:\n    57\t   A. Stop the line with the inconclusive verdict.\n    58\t   B. Re-draw control-1 from scratch under the current rules (about $0.85, a new ceiling; the same risk again).\n    59\t   C. Resume control-1 from 09-08 under the candidate rule (about $0.15 inside the current ceiling), then read pair 1 as registered.\n    60\t   Which one, and what result of it would move the decision? If C, is it legitimate for pair 1 given that I have seen control-1's\n    61\t   lead count (item 5) but not linked-1's P rows?\n    62\t5. Should the id copy error itself go to Alex as a product finding (one structural rule), and what would that rule be (for example,\n    63\t   evidence cited by a short list position the code maps back, or the retry note naming the nearest listed ids)? It is a change to the\n    64\t   frozen judge, a new version only Alex opens.\n9:The theme block (D191, D195): an asset thesis is judged with every open, judged theme thesis in view and answers, in theme_pushes,\n10:which way each theme it weighed pushes it; theme theses are judged before asset theses in a round, and a theme judgement that says\n49:    basis = {evidence_id for j in recent for evidence_id in j['cites']}\n57:    pushes = PUSHES\n60:        'required': ['rung', 'reasons', 'cites', 'cites_views', 'pushes', 'changed', 'why_changed'],\n63:            'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}, 'cites_views': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}},\n64:            'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence_id', 'push'],\n65:                                                  'properties': {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}},\n69:    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\n70:    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\n71:                                                                       'properties': {'view_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}}\n180:    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n181:                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n182:                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n221:    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\n223:            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\n235:    for cited in data['cites']:\n238:    for cited in data['cites_views']:\n     1\t# Current state\n     2\t\n     3\t**Clean Steps 1–3, current (2026-11-11).** Records: Step 1, [round log](../clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md) §§16–47; Step 2, [Step 2 log](../clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md) §§12–19.\n     4\t- **Step 1 configuration: c8, adopted by Alex (D387).** It runs DeepSeek Flash at high effort, with a 64,000-token output cap; a\n     5\t  format failure or a cut answer is resent once (D380). It carries Alex's decisions D382–D385:\n     6\t  - figures are conditions;\n     7\t  - material statements with no thesis are kept without links;\n     8\t  - only big matters open a thesis;\n     9\t  - no target prices.\n    10\t\n    11\t  [PRD §12](../clean-arch/PRD.md) holds its system prompt, closing check and schema; a run with no candidate files sends exactly the\n    12\t  accepted request.\n    13\t- **Acceptance (D386, [protocol](../clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/ACCEPTANCE-PROTOCOL.md)).** 50 fresh articles that no run,\n    14\t  old or new, had used: news from 2026-09-05 to 09-07, a holiday weekend with no NVIDIA posts. One draw; two readers and a third on\n    15\t  disputes.\n    16\t  - helpful 132/139 (core 83/83);\n    17\t  - wrongly opened theses 1 of 10;\n    18\t  - search 141/143 available repeat pairs, or 141/145 for the whole system (one 11-article story supplies 55 pairs, and revisions are\n    19\t    barely exercised);\n    20\t  - clear wrong merges 1/57, plus 2 overlaps;\n    21\t  - detail retention 22 = 22. This is a storage comparison: every record keeps its own text. It is not a usability test.\n    22\t\n    23\t  Dev ×3 on the frozen golden-v5 (a lead): helpful 214, 211 and 212 of 234; search 98.9–100%; clear wrong merges about 1%. Step 1\n    24\t  cost for the fresh set plus dev ×3: $4.20 at published rates.\n    25\t- **Steps 2 and 3** are built in isolation (`clean-arch/step2`, `clean-arch/step3`): search, comparison, grouping and later linking.\n    26\t  They are not integrated with production storage. **Step 4 (judging) has not passed** on the clean path: its ladder step is built and\n    27\t  measured (four Stage A runs, lines missed by 1 to 3 answers; D426), so nothing yet shows the clean system can judge an investment\n    28\t  view on its own questions.\n    29\t- **Step 2 is closed and frozen (Alex, D427, 2026-11-11;** [Step 2 log](../clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md) §§14–19**).** It goes\n    30\t  to production only with the whole clean path, after Step 4 meets its lines; `tests/test_frozen_clean_step2.py` guards its files. Its three lines were met at the acceptance above (one draw; \"later version\"\n    31\t  relations barely exercised), and no miss of the seeded end-to-end test (clean 18, 18, 17 against production 17, 15, 16) has\n    32\t  been traced to it (the two single-draw misses were diagnosed on 2026-11-11, below: neither traces to Step 2). What happened since the close-out of 2026-11-08:\n    33\t  - A change to Jev's wording for \"later version\" relations failed its line (42 calls, 2026-11-09) and tuning stopped.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from collections import Counter\nimport json,pathlib,re,sqlite3,sys\nsys.path[:0]=['\\\\''src'\\\\'','\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window'\\\\'']\nfrom hivemind.views import judging\ndef op(p):\n c=sqlite3.connect(pathlib.Path(p).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\nbase=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]); arc=op(base/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\''); v=op(base/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\nids=('\\\\''e362'\\\\'','\\\\''e3620'\\\\'','\\\\''e3110'\\\\'','\\\\''e3111'\\\\'','\\\\''e3112'\\\\'','\\\\''e393'\\\\'')\nprint('\\\\''existing ledger evidence:'\\\\'',[tuple(x) for x in v.execute('\\\\''select evidence_id, created_seq, quote from evidence where evidence_id in (?,?,?,?,?,?)'\\\\'',ids)])\ns=json.loads((base/'\\\\''summary.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nfor ident in (8807,8809,8938,8941):\n r=arc.execute('\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(ident,)).fetchone()\n x=json.loads(r['\\\\''request_json'\\\\''])\n print(ident,'\\\\''messages'\\\\'',[(m['\\\\''role'\\\\''],len(m['\\\\''content'\\\\''])) for m in x['\\\\''messages'\\\\'']])\n print(ident,'\\\\''tag appearances'\\\\'',[ (tag,[line[:220] for line in x['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\''].splitlines() if re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\b'\\\\''+tag+r'\\\\''\\\\b'\\\\'',line)]) for tag in ids if re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\b'\\\\''+tag+r'\\\\''\\\\b'\\\\'',x['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\''])])\n a=json.loads(r['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\''])\n print(ident,'\\\\''rung'\\\\'',a['\\\\''rung'\\\\''],'\\\\''changed'\\\\'',a['\\\\''changed'\\\\''],'\\\\''errors evidence'\\\\'',[(p['\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\''],p) for p in a['\\\\''pushes'\\\\''] if p['\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\''] in ids], '\\\\''investigated reason'\\\\'', a['\\\\''reasons'\\\\''][:1000] if ident in (8938,8941) else '\\\\'''\\\\'')\n print(ident,'\\\\''provider raw shape'\\\\'',list(json.loads(r['\\\\''response_json'\\\\''])))\n if ident not in (8938,8941):continue\n mem=sqlite3.connect('\\\\'':memory:'\\\\''); mem.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n v.backup(mem)\n mem.execute('\\\\''delete from judgements where seq>=1518 and view_id=?'\\\\'',('\\\\''v21'\\\\'',))\n print('\\\\''actual check'\\\\'',judging.check_answer(mem,'\\\\''v21'\\\\'',a,x['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']))\n for dst in (('\\\\''e3620'\\\\'',) if ident==8938 else ('\\\\''e3110'\\\\'','\\\\''e3112'\\\\'')):\n  src='\\\\''e362'\\\\'' if ident == 8938 else '\\\\''e3111'\\\\''\n  test=json.loads(r['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\''])\n  test['\\\\''cites'\\\\'']=[dst if i==src else i for i in test['\\\\''cites'\\\\'']]\n  for push in test['\\\\''pushes'\\\\'']:\n   if push['\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\'']==src: push['\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\'']=dst\n  print('\\\\''check on copy substitutions'\\\\'',src,dst,judging.check_answer(mem,'\\\\''v21'\\\\'',test,x['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']))\nprint('\\\\''same-day written H2 facts check'\\\\'')\nold=op('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'')\nfor name,columns,seq in [('\\\\''views'\\\\'','\\\\''view_id,question,created_seq'\\\\'','\\\\''created_seq'\\\\''),('\\\\''evidence'\\\\'','\\\\''evidence_id,quote,created_seq'\\\\'','\\\\''created_seq'\\\\''),('\\\\''evidence_links'\\\\'','\\\\''evidence_id,view_id,seq'\\\\'','\\\\''seq'\\\\''),('\\\\''view_switches'\\\\'','\\\\''view_id,open,reason,after_seq'\\\\'','\\\\''after_seq'\\\\''),('\\\\''successions'\\\\'','\\\\''view_id,succeeds,seq'\\\\'','\\\\''seq'\\\\'')]:\n query=f'\\\\''select {columns} from {name}'\\\\''\n built=Counter(tuple(row) for row in v.execute(query))\n same=Counter(tuple(row) for row in old.execute(query+'\\\\'' where '\\\\''+seq+'\\\\'' <=1518'\\\\''))\n full=Counter(tuple(row) for row in old.execute(query))\n print(name,len(built),len(same),len(full),'\\\\''equal through 09-08 seq'\\\\'',built==same,'\\\\''extras vs complete'\\\\'',sum((built-full).values()))\nfor name,columns in [('\\\\''view_keys'\\\\'','\\\\''view_id,measure,scope,period_start,period_end,unit'\\\\''),('\\\\''rungs'\\\\'','\\\\''view_id,position,label,condition,lo,hi'\\\\''),\n ('\\\\''judgements'\\\\'','\\\\''view_id, publication_day, rung, reasons, reference, implied_outcome, cited_evidence_json, cited_views_json, pushes_json, theme_pushes_json, changed, why_changed, request_sha256'\\\\'')]:\n query=f'\\\\''select {columns} from {name}'\\\\''\n if name=='\\\\''judgements'\\\\'':query+=\\\" where view_id not in ('\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'')\\\"\n built=Counter(tuple(row) for row in v.execute(query))\n full=Counter(tuple(row) for row in old.execute(query))\n print(name,len(built),len(full),'\\\\''extras vs complete'\\\\'',sum((built-full).values()),'\\\\''missing vs complete'\\\\'',sum((full-built).values()))\nprint('\\\\''copied historical nonreader rows'\\\\'',[(r['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],r['\\\\''view'\\\\''],r['\\\\''day'\\\\''],r['\\\\''refused'\\\\'']) for r in s['\\\\''archive judge rows written (dated)'\\\\''] if not r['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']])\nprint('\\\\''view judgement links H2 how are missing accounted'\\\\'', [tuple(r) for r in v.execute(\\\"select day,seq from days_completed order by seq desc limit 1\\\")],[tuple(r) for r in old.execute(\\\"select day,seq from days_completed where day>'\\\\''2026-09-07'\\\\'' order by seq\\\")])\n' '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/control-1-copy'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
