\\\\'',built==same,'\\\\''extras vs complete'\\\\'',sum((built-full).values()))\nfor name,columns in [('\\\\''view_keys'\\\\'','\\\\''view_id,measure,scope,period_start,period_end,unit'\\\\''),('\\\\''rungs'\\\\'','\\\\''view_id,position,label,condition,lo,hi'\\\\''),\n ('\\\\''judgements'\\\\'','\\\\''view_id, publication_day, rung, reasons, reference, implied_outcome, cited_evidence_json, cited_views_json, pushes_json, theme_pushes_json, changed, why_changed, request_sha256'\\\\'')]:\n query=f'\\\\''select {columns} from {name}'\\\\''\n if name=='\\\\''judgements'\\\\'':query+=\\\" where view_id not in ('\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'')\\\"\n built=Counter(tuple(row) for row in v.execute(query))\n full=Counter(tuple(row) for row in old.execute(query))\n print(name,len(built),len(full),'\\\\''extras vs complete'\\\\'',sum((built-full).values()),'\\\\''missing vs complete'\\\\'',sum((full-built).values()))\nprint('\\\\''copied historical nonreader rows'\\\\'',[(r['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],r['\\\\''view'\\\\''],r['\\\\''day'\\\\''],r['\\\\''refused'\\\\'']) for r in s['\\\\''archive judge rows written (dated)'\\\\''] if not r['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']])\nprint('\\\\''view judgement links H2 how are missing accounted'\\\\'', [tuple(r) for r in v.execute(\\\"select day,seq from days_completed order by seq desc limit 1\\\")],[tuple(r) for r in old.execute(\\\"select day,seq from days_completed where day>'\\\\''2026-09-07'\\\\'' order by seq\\\")])\n' '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/control-1-copy'\"","aggregated_output":"existing ledger evidence: [('e3110', 1168, 'if something goes wrong at either lab, cheaper Chinese open-weight models could spark a price war across the industry.'), ('e3111', 1168, \"It signed deals with Apollo, Blackstone, BlackRock, Brookfield, Goldman Sachs, and KKR to mobilize over $500 billion in third-party AI financing, with CEO Jensen Huang capping Nvidia's exposure at roughly 25% per project.\"), ('e3112', 1168, \"Michael Burry argues Nvidia's own customer base carries a version of Eisman's concentration risk. He has focused on Nvidia's reliance on a small group of hyperscale customers, including Microsoft, Meta, Amazon, and Alphabet, warning a pullback from even one could meaningfully hurt revenue.\"), ('e362', 237, '“Nvidia chips are essential for training,” Dimmich said. “For this type of inference compute, increasingly there are ASIC [application-specific integrated circuit] designs that are cheaper than Nvidia but still need foundry capacity at TSMC.”'), ('e3620', 1304, \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 and 2028 revenues indicates year-over-year growth of 85.4% and 2.2%, respectively.\"), ('e393', 246, 'Fujifilm has commercialized Japan’s first whole-body CT system powered by NVIDIA Blackwell, using diffusion-based deep learning reconstruction to improve image quality.')]\n8807 messages [('system', 4924), ('user', 66060)]\n8807 tag appearances []\n8807 rung 2 changed True errors evidence [('e393', {'evidence_id': 'e393', 'push': 'toward_first'})] investigated reason \n8807 provider raw shape ['id', 'object', 'created', 'model', 'choices', 'usage', 'service_tier', 'system_fingerprint']\n8809 messages [('system', 4924), ('user', 66250)]\n8809 tag appearances [('e393', ['The code returned the previous answer because: e393 is not among the evidence shown to v14; push on e393 which was not shown to v14'])]\n8809 rung 2 changed True errors evidence [] investigated reason \n8809 provider raw shape ['id', 'object', 'created', 'model', 'choices', 'usage', 'service_tier', 'system_fingerprint']\n8938 messages [('system', 4924), ('user', 20443)]\n8938 tag appearances [('e3620', ['- e3620 [third_party_view; Zacks.com (analyst); original source Zacks.com 2026-09-01; from gnews:393f041679180b7d31179e8f 2026-09-01] Zacks consensus estimated NVIDIA total revenue growth of 85.4% in FY2027 and 2.2% in F']), ('e3110', ['- e3110 [third_party_view; InsiderMonkey, recounting Steve Eisman’s remarks on CNBC’s Fast Money; original source Steve Eisman 2026-08-13; from gnews:afc4112f1dd4c804f27af950 2026-08-28] Steve Eisman warned that problems']), ('e3112', ['- e3112 [third_party_view; InsiderMonkey, recounting Michael Burry’s view; original source Michael Burry ; from gnews:afc4112f1dd4c804f27af950 2026-08-28] Michael Burry warned that NVIDIA’s reliance on Microsoft, Meta, A'])]\n8938 rung 1 changed True errors evidence [('e3110', {'evidence_id': 'e3110', 'push': 'toward_last'}), ('e3112', {'evidence_id': 'e3112', 'push': 'toward_last'}), ('e362', {'evidence_id': 'e362', 'push': 'toward_first'})] investigated reason The latest explicit Wall Street expectation is 45% growth, which sits at rung 3; earlier estimates of 83% and 85.4% sit at rung 1. The operating run-rate points substantially above either reference: FY2027 Q1 and Q2 revenue plus Q3 guidance total $285.8 billion; carrying the Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate of about 12.3% into Q4 implies roughly $121.3 billion for Q4 and about $407.1 billion for FY2027, or 88.5% growth from FY2026's $215.94 billion. NVIDIA's stated 70% full-year growth outlook implies about $367 billion, but after the first three quarters it would require Q4 revenue of only about $81 billion—below Q3 guidance—so it does not outweigh the run-rate indicated by the current-quarter guidance. The implied growth remains above the 60% rung-1 boundary.\n8938 provider raw shape ['id', 'object', 'created', 'model', 'choices', 'usage', 'service_tier', 'system_fingerprint']\nactual check ['e362 is not among the evidence shown to v21', 'push on e362 which was not shown to v21']\ncheck on copy substitutions e362 e3620 []\n8941 messages [('system', 4924), ('user', 20633)]\n8941 tag appearances [('e362', ['The code returned the previous answer because: e362 is not among the evidence shown to v21; push on e362 which was not shown to v21']), ('e3620', ['- e3620 [third_party_view; Zacks.com (analyst); original source Zacks.com 2026-09-01; from gnews:393f041679180b7d31179e8f 2026-09-01] Zacks consensus estimated NVIDIA total revenue growth of 85.4% in FY2027 and 2.2% in F']), ('e3110', ['- e3110 [third_party_view; InsiderMonkey, recounting Steve Eisman’s remarks on CNBC’s Fast Money; original source Steve Eisman 2026-08-13; from gnews:afc4112f1dd4c804f27af950 2026-08-28] Steve Eisman warned that problems']), ('e3112', ['- e3112 [third_party_view; InsiderMonkey, recounting Michael Burry’s view; original source Michael Burry ; from gnews:afc4112f1dd4c804f27af950 2026-08-28] Michael Burry warned that NVIDIA’s reliance on Microsoft, Meta, A'])]\n8941 rung 1 changed True errors evidence [('e3111', {'evidence_id': 'e3111', 'push': 'toward_last'}), ('e3112', {'evidence_id': 'e3112', 'push': 'toward_last'})] investigated reason The latest specifically stated Wall Street expectation is 45% growth, which is rung 3; the older cited 42% estimate is also rung 3. Other estimates differ materially: LSEG's 83% estimate is rung 1. NVIDIA's stated 70% full-year growth outlook is rung 1. The reported FY2027 Q1 and Q2 revenue plus Q3 guidance total $285.8 billion; carrying the 12.3% sequential growth from Q2 to Q3 into Q4 implies about $121.3 billion for Q4 and roughly $407.1 billion for FY2027, or 88.5% growth from FY2026 revenue. That is above the rung-1 threshold of 60%. The 70% annual outlook is a lower but still rung-1 input; a 70% full-year outcome would require Q4 revenue of only about $81.3 billion after the first three quarters, well below the momentum implied by Q3 guidance. Unquantified downside risks do not outweigh the reported results and current-quarter guidance.\n8941 provider raw shape ['id', 'object', 'created', 'model', 'choices', 'usage', 'service_tier', 'system_fingerprint']\nactual check ['e3111 is not among the evidence shown to v21', 'push on e3111 which was not shown to v21']\ncheck on copy substitutions e3111 e3110 