{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections,json,pathlib,sqlite3,sys\nsys.path.insert(0,'\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window'\\\\'')\nimport contradictions\nfolder=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])\ndef op(p): return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\nc=op(folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\na=op(folder/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'')\ns=json.loads((folder/'\\\\''summary.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nfor _,grp in list(collections.defaultdict(list).items()): pass\npairs={}\nfor date,cls,segment,company,segment_text,company_text in contradictions.daily(c,'\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-07'\\\\''):\n if cls=='\\\\''definite'\\\\'': pairs.setdefault((segment_text,company_text),[]).append((date,segment,company))\nfor (segment_text,company_text),days in list(pairs.items())[:5]:\n print(days)\n print('\\\\''Data Center:'\\\\'',segment_text)\n print('\\\\''Total revenue:'\\\\'',company_text)\nold=op(pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\''))\nolda=op(pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite'\\\\''))\ncosts=dict(olda.execute(\\\"select call_id,cost_usd from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\''\\\"))\nremaining=list(old.execute(\\\"select view_id,publication_day,call_id from judgements where publication_day between '\\\\''2026-09-08'\\\\'' and '\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\'' and view_id in ('\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'')\\\"))\nprint('\\\\''old-2 remaining reader acceptances after Sep7'\\\\'',collections.Counter(v for v,_,_ in remaining),sum(costs[id] for _,_,id in remaining))\nprint('\\\\''old-2 remaining reader acceptances after Sep8'\\\\'',sum(day>'\\\\''2026-09-08'\\\\'' for _,day,_ in remaining),sum(costs[id] for _,day,id in remaining if day>'\\\\''2026-09-08'\\\\''))\nprint('\\\\''Day Sep8 old reader costs:'\\\\'',[(v,id,costs[id]) for v,day,id in remaining if day=='\\\\''2026-09-08'\\\\''])\n' '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/control-1-copy'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections,json,pathlib,sqlite3,sys\nsys.path.insert(0,'\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window'\\\\'')\nimport contradictions\nfolder=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])\ndef op(p): return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\nc=op(folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\na=op(folder/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'')\ns=json.loads((folder/'\\\\''summary.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nfor _,grp in list(collections.defaultdict(list).items()): pass\npairs={}\nfor date,cls,segment,company,segment_text,company_text in contradictions.daily(c,'\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-07'\\\\''):\n if cls=='\\\\''definite'\\\\'': pairs.setdefault((segment_text,company_text),[]).append((date,segment,company))\nfor (segment_text,company_text),days in list(pairs.items())[:5]:\n print(days)\n print('\\\\''Data Center:'\\\\'',segment_text)\n print('\\\\''Total revenue:'\\\\'',company_text)\nold=op(pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\''))\nolda=op(pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite'\\\\''))\ncosts=dict(olda.execute(\\\"select call_id,cost_usd from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\''\\\"))\nremaining=list(old.execute(\\\"select view_id,publication_day,call_id from judgements where publication_day between '\\\\''2026-09-08'\\\\'' and '\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\'' and view_id in ('\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'')\\\"))\nprint('\\\\''old-2 remaining reader acceptances after Sep7'\\\\'',collections.Counter(v for v,_,_ in remaining),sum(costs[id] for _,_,id in remaining))\nprint('\\\\''old-2 remaining reader acceptances after Sep8'\\\\'',sum(day>'\\\\''2026-09-08'\\\\'' for _,day,_ in remaining),sum(costs[id] for _,day,id in remaining if day>'\\\\''2026-09-08'\\\\''))\nprint('\\\\''Day Sep8 old reader costs:'\\\\'',[(v,id,costs[id]) for v,day,id in remaining if day=='\\\\''2026-09-08'\\\\''])\n' '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/control-1-copy'\"","aggregated_output":"[('2026-07-13', (390.0, 390.0, 'year'), (387.0, 387.0, 'leading'))]\nData Center: About $390 billion for FY2027. The $91 billion Q2 total-revenue guide implies an approximately $84 billion Data Center proxy at Q1’s 92% mix; carrying strong sequential growth forward and allowing for management’s Q2 growth-acceleration guidance and quantified demand supports a modest uplift from the roughly $380 billion prior estimate, while remaining below $400 billion.\nTotal revenue: About $387 billion: starting with reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 guidance of $91 billion, the roughly 11.5% sequential increase carried forward implies approximately $101.5 billion in Q3 and $113.1 billion in Q4. The resulting FY2027 total stays below $400 billion.\n[('2026-07-14', (400.0, 400.0, 'year'), (387.0, 387.0, 'leading'))]\nData Center: Roughly $400B for FY2027. FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B grown by Q1's 92% year-over-year rate implies about $372B; Q2's stated growth acceleration and the demand outlook support a modest further increase, while the $1T Blackwell/Vera Rubin visibility spans multiple products and calendar years and is not counted in full.\nTotal revenue: Approximately $387 billion: start with Q1’s $81.6 billion actual and Q2’s $91 billion guidance, then carry the roughly 11.5% sequential increase into Q3 and Q4, yielding about $101.5 billion and $113.1 billion. The four-quarter total is about $387 billion, below the $400 billion boundary.\n[('2026-07-15', (400.0, 400.0, 'year'), (387.0, 387.0, 'year'))]\nData Center: About $400B for FY2027. FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at Q1 FY2027's 92% year-over-year growth implies about $372B; management's Q2 growth-acceleration guidance and stronger demand evidence justify a modest uplift to the rung-2 boundary, while the multi-year, multi-product $1T visibility figure is discounted.\nTotal revenue: About $387B: carrying the Q1-to-Q2 sequential increase from $81.6B to the $91B Q2 guide forward gives roughly $101.5B in Q3 and $113.2B in Q4, for about $387B across FY2027.\n[('2026-07-17', (372.0, 372.0, 'year'), (244.0, 244.0, 'year'))]\nData Center: FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at the latest 92% year-over-year growth rate implies about $372B for FY2027; Q2 guidance for accelerating Data Center growth and the demand signals support a modest uplift to roughly $410B. This is above the $400B rung boundary but below $450B.\nTotal revenue: Approximately $417 billion: FY2026 revenue was $215.9 billion; Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion at 85.2% growth implies about $44.1 billion for the prior-year quarter, and the $91 billion Q2 guide at 95% growth implies about $46.7 billion. Applying 95% growth to the remaining FY2026 revenue gives about $244 billion for FY2027 Q3–Q4, for a total near $417 billion.\n[('2026-07-25', (385.0, 385.0, 'year'), (215.9, 215.9, 'year'))]\nData Center: Approximately $385B for FY2027: start with $75.25B in Q1, estimate Q2 at about $84B using the $91B total-revenue guidance and Q1's 92% Data Center mix, then carry the 21% sequential Data Center growth rate through Q3 and Q4. This is below $400B and above $350B.\nTotal revenue: Approximately $400–405 billion: FY2026 revenue was $215.9 billion, while FY2027 Q1 grew 85.2% year over year and Q2 guidance is $91 billion, up 95% year over year. Carrying forward strong near-term growth with some deceleration supports a modest lift over the $393 billion reference.\nold-2 remaining reader acceptances after Sep7 Counter({'v14': 13, 'v16': 13, 'v21': 13, 'v9': 13}) 0.182716\nold-2 remaining reader acceptances after Sep8 48 0.16901\nDay Sep8 old reader costs: [('v14', 7058, 0.003154), ('v16', 7069, 0.003412), ('v21', 7064, 0.002506), ('v9', 7072, 0.004634)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
