{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid-dry-linked-1.log; rg -n 'judge|days|spend|retry' docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md | head -25; sed -n '448,457p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"sequence\": \"linked-1\",\n \"terminal\": {\n  \"outcome\": \"complete\"\n },\n \"stopped\": \"\",\n \"bought (admitted attempts)\": 266,\n \"snapshot checks\": 266,\n \"window completed, no stop\": true,\n \"calendar completed (every day old-2 completed)\": true,\n \"committed graph equals the pinned one (labels included)\": true,\n \"probe jobs consumed exactly the pinned set\": true,\n \"every post-link reader judgement fresh on its own day\": true,\n \"every pre-link reader judgement from the archive\": true,\n \"reader judgements present\": true,\n \"upstream snapshot clean\": true,\n \"upstream snapshot exercised (linked)\": true,\n \"fixed trajectory (H2)\": true,\n \"ledger clean (not stopped, no overrun)\": true,\n \"accepted\": true\n}\nexit 0\n9:  (07-15), v21 (07-26) in every draw; the controls retire 247 rows (v14 71, v9 70, v16 56, v21 50), each reader's archive judge rows from\n10:  its first retired call on checked equal to its accepted judgements from its link day (no refused first attempt among readers).\n11:- `paid-dry-{linked,control}-{1,2,3}.log` (a marker judge for every bought judgement, every answer \"changed\", so propagation is at its\n13:  reader judgement fresh (call id above the copied archive's top) and every pre-link one from the archive; the upstream snapshot check\n14:  run on every linked reader request (267 in linked-1) with no problem; the fixed trajectory (H2) holds (non-reader judgements and every\n15:  other table equal to old-2's). Bought: 266 per linked sequence (19 days added by propagation), 247 per control.\n16:- `paid-dry-refused-upstream.log`: v14's first attempt on its third judgement refused (an evidence id it was not shown), its retry\n17:  accepted; no request shows the refused answer; 267 bought (the retry); snapshot checks clean.\n40:   freshness; the snapshot; H2. `send` exits non-zero when it fails. The judging day is bound inside `round.judge_day` and cleared when\n41:   it returns; a request is admitted only when its schema is `judgement` (unit check: a request titled \"Thesis v14\" without it, sent\n43:2. **Decisive checks:** freshness is now \"the accepted judgement's call was made during its own day's judging\" (the archive's top before\n44:   and after each `judge_day`; unit check: a call in another day's window fails); the snapshot compares each dependency entry, found by\n45:   its own target id, line for line with that target's recorded judgement day, comparison point, forecast and reasons excerpt, and the\n47:   substantive judgement field (pushes, theme pushes, why changed).\n48:3. **Stop paths, typed:** each sequence records every judge attempt at the transport (reader, day, request hash, retry, admitted) and\n49:   every judge row written with its day, and a terminal outcome (`complete`, `double refusal` with the reader and day, or `infrastructure\n50:   stop` with its reason). Exercised: `paid-double-refusal-linked.log` and `-control.log` (v9 refused twice on its second judgement:\n55:   with the exact requests, the read judgement ids shown and the paired control's conclusion in force (H4), the seven fixed dates (H5),\n79:   unexpected or unread row; H1 from the summaries' dated judge rows on matched reader-days; H3 (a linked grounding error unmatched by\n83:   judgements shown with their own requests (the trace), and the paired arm's conclusion in force; H3 now includes every reader's\n91:rows (fail), four extra refusals on matched reader-days (H1 fail) and three (tolerated: pass). Two of my own check fixtures were wrong on\n92:their first run (the H1 days not matched, then packet files overwritten by an earlier case) and were corrected; the code under test did\n97:  duplicate rows; a quantified CPU correction stored once per company judgement); completion inferred from replay returning; reading\n99:- Fixed for the pilot: the gate checks the completed calendar against the pinned one (`planned_days`, fixed apart from the replay's\n101:  pairs (a substituted judgement, a shifted span, a missing or duplicated row); `gain_credit` refuses a material failure without its\n**The one next task (D709, 2026-11-21): Alex's ceiling for the pilot of the paid whole-window comparison (pair 1: linked-1 and\ncontrol-1, estimate $1.96, $2.50 proposed)** (`research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md` §8, `PAID-BUILD.md`;\nproduction-readiness bullet below). Alex chose A (D699), the link census (D700) and the probe of a sharpened wording (D703). Done at\n$0.0575 so far: the census and the version-2 probe passed their gates (D702, D705); poc-v120 (link questions version 2) built and passed\nreview as a product configuration (D706; suite 380, mutants 14/14, every probe request rebuilt byte for byte); the paid design passed\n(D707, version 7); council reflection chose a one-pair pilot before the full comparison (D708); the pilot's harness, worksheet and\nverdict passed review (D709; 43 end-to-end checks; six dry sequences accepted; mutants and stop paths caught). The attainable verdict:\nthe stored v118 draws show Data Center above total revenue on 11, 56 and 1 dates. The full comparison (pairs 2 and 3, about $3.9 more,\nand 18–30 reviewer-hours of reading) follows only if pair 1 improves (D708).\n- **Production readiness (council P, consensus, $0; [RESULT.md](research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/RESULT.md)):** not ready for\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,re,sqlite3,sys,types\nsys.path[:0]=['\\\\''src'\\\\'','\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window'\\\\'']\nimport paid_run\nfrom hivemind.views import judging,round as rounds\nfolder=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])\ndef op(p): return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\ndisk=op(folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\''); mem=sqlite3.connect('\\\\'':memory:'\\\\''); mem.row_factory=sqlite3.Row; disk.backup(mem)\narc=op(folder/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\''); arc.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\nby_text={}\nfor row in arc.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_json,answer_json,request_sha256 from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\''\\\"):\n request=json.loads(row['\\\\''request_json'\\\\'']); system,user=(m['\\\\''content'\\\\''] for m in request['\\\\''messages'\\\\''])\n by_text.setdefault((system,user),[]).append(row)\ncfg=paid_run.config.load(str(paid_run.V118))\nobserved=[]\ndef archive_only(archive,cfg,settings,system,user,schema,name,purpose,transport=None):\n view=re.match(r'\\\\''Thesis (v\\\\d+) '\\\\'',user).group(1)\n entries=by_text[system,user]\n if view=='\\\\''v21'\\\\'':\n  row,= [r for r in entries if r['\\\\''call_id'\\\\'']==8938]\n  a=json.loads(row['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\''])\n  a['\\\\''cites'\\\\'']=['\\\\''e3620'\\\\'' if ref=='\\\\''e362'\\\\'' else ref for ref in a['\\\\''cites'\\\\'']]\n  for push in a['\\\\''pushes'\\\\'']:\n   if push['\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\'']=='\\\\''e362'\\\\'': push['\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\'']='\\\\''e3620'\\\\''\n  observed.append((view,'\\\\''same request as 8938, corrected answer injected in memory'\\\\''))\n  return types.SimpleNamespace(data=a,call_id=8942,request_sha256=row['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''].split('\\\\'':refused:'\\\\'')[0],cost_usd=0,cached=False)\n row,=[r for r in entries if '\\\\'':refused:'\\\\'' not in r['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''] and '\\\\'':retired:'\\\\'' not in r['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\'']]\n observed.append((view,'\\\\''exact cached request'\\\\'',row['\\\\''call_id'\\\\'']))\n return types.SimpleNamespace(data=json.loads(row['\\\\''answer_json'\\\\'']),call_id=row['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],request_sha256=row['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''],cost_usd=0,cached=True)\ndef test_transport(*args): raise AssertionError('\\\\''transport is disabled for the offline check'\\\\'')\njudging.model.call=archive_only\nmarker=rounds.judge_day(mem, None,cfg,'\\\\''2026-09-08'\\\\'',1518,transport=test_transport)\nprint('\\\\''result'\\\\'',marker)\nprint('\\\\''requests'\\\\'',sorted(observed))\nprint('\\\\''day 09-08 commits'\\\\'', [tuple(r) for r in mem.execute(\\\"select view_id,call_id from judgements where seq=1518 order by judgement_id\\\")])\nprint('\\\\''day 09-08 processing marks'\\\\'',[tuple(r) for r in mem.execute(\\\"select result,reason from processing_steps where input_id='\\\\''day:2026-09-08'\\\\''\\\")])\nprint('\\\\''disk day 09-08 judgements still:'\\\\'',disk.execute(\\\"select count(*) from judgements where seq=1518\\\").fetchone()[0])\n' '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/control-1-copy'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
