e refusal in some sequence of six is not rare. Should the rule for the remaining comparison change, and to what?\n    53\t   Candidate (mine): on a double refusal in either arm, the day is resumed once, as the product does (the refused rows retired, the\n    54\t   refusals counted in H1); a second double refusal on the same day is terminal under the old precedence. Recorded before any further\n    55\t   send. Counter-arguments: selection, a rule changed after a result, the symmetry between arms.\n    56\t4. The next step for Alex (he is active; any spend beyond the $2.50 ceiling is his). Options I see:\n    57\t   A. Stop the line with the inconclusive verdict.\n    58\t   B. Re-draw control-1 from scratch under the current rules (about $0.85, a new ceiling; the same risk again).\n    59\t   C. Resume control-1 from 09-08 under the candidate rule (about $0.15 inside the current ceiling), then read pair 1 as registered.\n    60\t   Which one, and what result of it would move the decision? If C, is it legitimate for pair 1 given that I have seen control-1's\n    61\t   lead count (item 5) but not linked-1's P rows?\n    62\t5. Should the id copy error itself go to Alex as a product finding (one structural rule), and what would that rule be (for example,\n    63\t   evidence cited by a short list position the code maps back, or the retry note naming the nearest listed ids)? It is a change to the\n    64\t   frozen judge, a new version only Alex opens.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"agent_message","text":"**Close pair 1 as inconclusive and stop the registered comparison (A).** Linked-1 completed and passed the run checks. Control-1 stopped on September 8 after two answers named evidence outside the list they were given. The two runs spent **$1.70 of the $2.50 ceiling**. [Linked-1 launcher log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-pilot-2026-11-21/linked-1.log:1)\n\n1. **The registered verdict is inconclusive.** A linked double refusal would have taken precedence and failed the pilot. The linked run completed, so the control’s double refusal decides it. The verdict code returns “invalid or incomplete” before it opens the forecast readings. “Control double refusal” is the specific reason to record. [Registered precedence](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:136) · [Pilot verdict code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:348)\n\n2. **The refusals came from invalid evidence tags.** Call 8938 returned 29 citations, of which 28 matched the 29 shown. It used `e362` in both its citations and its evidence assessments, omitted `e3620`, and discussed the 85.4% estimate carried by `e3620`. The retry corrected the first bad tag, returned **13** citations, and used `e3111` in both places. That tag is one character away from both `e3110` and `e3112`. I replayed both answers through the product check. Those tags caused every refusal, and either substitution for `e3111` clears the check. The first case strongly supports a copy error. The retry’s intended source is less certain. Both answers forecast about $407.1 billion and 88.5% growth. The control had zero dependencies, and none of the 118 fresh Data Center and total-revenue requests mentioned the revenue-growth question. [Control archive, calls 8938 and 8941](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/control-1-copy/archive.sqlite) · [Retry and evidence checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:199)\n\n   | Stored run | Judge calls | Refused | What was refused |\n   |---|---:|---:|---|\n   | Old-1 | 1,610 | 1 | Theme tags in evidence citations |\n   | Old-2 | 1,620 | 4 | Three one-edit evidence tags and one theme-tag case |\n   | Old-3 | 1,709 | 2 | Two one-edit evidence tags |\n   | Control-1, fresh only | 201 | 3 | `e393` on 8807, then the two September 8 answers |\n\n   All seven historical retries passed. `e393` had no one-edit match among the 124 shown, and retry 8809 passed. The 201 fresh calls split 60/58/44/39 across v14/v9/v16/v21. The archive has 204 new judge entries because three non-reader answers were replayed from old-2, two already marked refused. [Census script](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/id_typo_census.py:12) · [Control summary](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/control-1-copy/summary.json)\n\n   Every table checked matched old-2 through September 7, including 984 non-reader judgements, 4,196 evidence entries and 5,223 evidence links. The full check found omissions starting on the unfinished September 8, with no differing entries among those present. I reproduced the parser’s **28 of 60 versus 50 of 60**. The contradiction genuinely recurred in the fresh control. On July 13 and 14, Data Center was forecast at about $390B and $400B against $387B for the whole company. The parser also flagged July 17 by taking a half-year subtotal as the annual figure, so 28 remains a lead. [Partial comparison script](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/h2_until_stop.py:15) · [Parser](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/contradictions.py:50)\n\n3. **Use one resume per run per day in a future, pre-registered comparison.** Apply it to both versions, keep the original refusals in the matched-day count, and use the old verdict order if the same day double-refuses again. The evidence establishes a real failure mode. It is too sparse to estimate how often six runs would hit it. In an offline replay of September 8, the product reused the archived Data Center and CPU answers and completed the day with one corrected revenue-growth answer supplied in memory. Before a new send, test both recovery and a second stop on stored data. The runner currently overwrites the first call range for a resumed date, so that test must prove that both refusals and earlier accepted answers keep their date. [Product resume path](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:305) · [Runner’s day tracking](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:238)\n\n4. **C is legitimate as exploratory work only.** I estimate about **$0.17 before retries** from old-2’s remaining calls. Keeping the linked forecasts blind helps, but the control stop and its forecast signal were already visible when the rule change was proposed. B also selects a replacement after seeing the first control stop and repeats the same failure risk. The result that would justify continuing is a **fresh pair under the rule agreed in advance**, with fewer contradictions after the blind gain review, no CPU double counting, and fewer than four extra linked refusals on matched days. [Registered pilot continuation rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:201)\n\n5. **Take the evidence-tag defect to Alex as one product finding.** In a new judge version he opens, give both citations and evidence assessments the same closed list of tags from that exact request. The judge still chooses which evidence matters. The code restricts which source each tag can identify. `e3111` shows why guessing the nearest tag is unsafe. The test should also check whether accepted citations point to the intended facts, since a valid tag can still name the wrong source. [Current answer format](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:55) · [Evidence membership check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:227)"}}
